invariant: INV-16
file: chacha20_vector.c
catches: chacha20_equiv_test
reason: the group loop XORs three of its four lanes, so the fourth block
  of every group keeps the input's bytes: in place, 64 bytes of each 256
  go out as plaintext. bin/chacha20_equiv_test compares every byte of the
  output with chacha20.c's, at every length that holds a whole group.

